  "chapter": {
    "number": 10,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(11 in KJV) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In the Lord I have put my trust: how will you⌃ say to my soul,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Flee to the mountains as a sparrow?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For behold the sinners have bent their bow, they have prepared their arrows for the quiver, to shoot",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 21
          },
          {
            "text": "privily at the upright in heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For they have pulled down what you did frame, but what has the righteous done?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is in his holy temple, as for the Lord, his throne is in heaven: his eyes look upon the poor, his eyelids try the sons of men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord tries the righteous and the ungodly: and he that loves unrighteousness hates his own soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall rain upon sinners snares, fire, and brimstone, and a stormy blast shall be the portion of their cup.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord is righteous, and loves",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 22
          },
          {
            "text": "righteousness; his face beholds uprightness.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 21,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. in dark moon, or little moonlight, q. d. luce malignâ",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 10,
          "verse": 3
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 22,
        "caller": "+",
